{
"cycle": 1,
"assessment": "The recent implementation covers the requested major items: DeckDesignOrderTrace, validateReviewArtifactDesignOrder, structured chart visual guidance, EVIDENCE_CLAIM_ALIGNMENT_GAP, and SEMANTIC_MOTIF_DRIFT are now present in code/tests/docs.    Remaining coherence risk is narrower: source-evidence provenance can be backfilled from chart-intent output, and the validator is still mostly top-level/deck-order oriented rather than artifact-aware for nested scientific chart reports and recipe catalogs. Microsoft’s chart-type reference reinforces that chart choice depends on data arrangement and chart purpose, so mdpr-skill should keep these as semantic review contracts rather than renderer choices. ([Microsoft 지원][1])",
"locally_actionable_todos": [
{
"title": "Prevent chart-intent refs from satisfying earlier source-evidence stage",
"why": "buildDeckDesignOrderTrace currently defaults source_evidence to chartIntentRefs when sourceEvidenceRefs are absent, which lets a later-stage chart-intent report make an earlier stage appear present. That weakens the declared order narrative_spine -> source_evidence -> slide_role -> chart_intent and can hide missing independent source evidence.  ",
"suggested_files": [
"packages/review-core/src/index.ts",
"tests/review-core-runtime.test.ts",
"docs/ppt-visual-validation.md",
"06_IR_CONTRACTS.md"
],
"acceptance": [
"buildDeckDesignOrderTrace no longer uses refs prefixed with chartIntent: as source_evidence.",
"If sourceEvidenceRefs are omitted but chartIntentReport exists, either mark source_evidence missing or derive only raw structural refs such as sheet, rows, columns, numericCells, formulaCells, chartFamilies, and errorBars with an explicit derived-source-evidence warning.",
"Add a finding such as DESIGN_ORDER_SOURCE_EVIDENCE_BACKFILLED or DESIGN_ORDER_SOURCE_EVIDENCE_MISSING_INDEPENDENTLY when source evidence is inferred from later chart artifacts.",
"Tests cover explicit sourceEvidenceRefs, chart-only input, and mixed chartIntentReport plus missing narrative/slide role without leaking raw values, coordinates, colors, or PPTX geometry."
]
},
{
"title": "Make validateReviewArtifactDesignOrder artifact-aware and nested",
"why": "The validator checks root-level evidenceRefs, entries, and a deck-stage designOrder, but scientific chart reports and high-need chart recipes store designOrder and evidence under nested intents/recipes. This can miss out-of-order scientific chart stages and can falsely treat valid nested evidence as missing.  ",
"suggested_files": [
"packages/review-core/src/index.ts",
"tests/review-core-runtime.test.ts",
"docs/ppt-visual-validation.md"
],
"acceptance": [
"validateReviewArtifactDesignOrder recognizes both deck order and scientific chart order: data_evidence -> scientific_chart_intent -> semantic_visual_guidance -> renderer_capability_request -> review_notes.",
"Validator scans nested intents[].designOrder, recipes[].designOrder, intents[].evidenceRefs, and recipe semantic/data-shape fields where appropriate.",
"Add tests where a ScientificChartIntentReport with scrambled nested designOrder emits DESIGN_ORDER_OUT_OF_SEQUENCE.",
"Add tests where a valid ScientificChartIntentReport does not emit REVIEW_ARTIFACT_EVIDENCE_MISSING solely because evidenceRefs are nested.",
"Boundary leakage detection remains recursive and still rejects final renderer fields."
]
}
],
"external_or_manual_todos": [
{
"title": "MDPR validation-ref producer contract",
"why_not_local": "mdpr-skill can require and consume mdpr_validation_refs, but MDPR owns parsing, rendering, layout, PPTX objects, and final pass/fail validation. "
},
{
"title": "Manual final visual approval",
"why_not_local": "Manual inspection is outside this local repo scope and should not become a mdpr-skill implementation gate."
}
],
"duplicates_or_rejected": [
"Do not re-add DeckDesignOrderTrace; it is already implemented.",
"Do not re-add validateReviewArtifactDesignOrder; only improve nested/artifact-aware coverage.",
"Do not re-add densityClass, labelBudgetClass, recommendedDownshift, aggregationRequired, or narrativeFit; they are already present.",
"Do not re-add EVIDENCE_CLAIM_ALIGNMENT_GAP or SEMANTIC_MOTIF_DRIFT; both are already implemented.",
"Rejected: raw XLSX ingestion, raw colors, fixed coordinates, PPTX geometry, renderer object IDs, and manual visual inspection as local TODOs."
]
}

[1]: https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/office/available-chart-types-in-office-a6187218-807e-4103-9e0a-27cdb19afb90 "Available chart types in Office | Microsoft Support"

